# CommunityOps console configuration
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. NEVER commit a real .env file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live mode (talks to the deployed AWS backend)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All three values come from the CloudFormation stack outputs:
#   aws cloudformation describe-stacks --stack-name CommunityOps \
#     --region ap-south-1 --query "Stacks[0].Outputs"

VITE_API_URL=
VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=
VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Federated sign-in (not available yet)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Federated sign-in is hard-disabled in this frontend until PKCE, state
# validation, callback exchange, and configured Cognito providers ship together.
# Stray VITE_AUTH_PROVIDERS or hosted-UI variables never render provider buttons.
# Do not set provider variables for this build.

# Fallback organization only. The console scopes requests to the organization it
# reads from the signed-in user's `cognito:groups` claim, so this value is used
# only when no session names one — before sign-in, or for an account that is in
# no organization group. Setting it grants nothing: the API authorizes every
# request against the caller's own groups and returns 403 otherwise.
VITE_ORG_ID=ORG-wemakedev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Capability flags
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A capability flag states whether the backend contract behind an area of the
# product exists. It is not a permission: access is decided by API Gateway and
# tenancy.authorize_organization, never by the console.
#
# Off unless the value is exactly "true". While a flag is off, the navigation
# entry is absent and the route resolves to the not-found view.
#
# AttendeeOps needs GET /events/{eventId}/attendees and seeded attendee records,
# neither of which exists yet.
# VITE_CAPABILITY_ATTENDEE_OPS=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Try Demo Account
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The login action calls anonymous POST /demo/session. The backend authenticates
# one fixed restricted identity and returns an ID token. The browser sends no
# identity or credential. Set VITE_API_URL to a deployment where demo access is
# enabled; the action reports a safe unavailable state otherwise.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Demo mode (local UI work with no backend)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not the same thing as "Try Demo Account" above, and the console keeps them
# apart on screen: this serves fabricated local records and shows an amber
# "Demo Mode" badge, while a demo *session* shows a neutral "Demo workspace" chip
# and every record in it is a real API response.
# Opt-in only. When true, the console serves built-in sample data and shows a
# "Demo Mode" badge. It is never used as a fallback for a failing backend.
# VITE_USE_MOCK=true
